orbit-tape (0.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * orbit-tape mcp: an MCP server for Claude with read-only market tools
    (candles, indicator runs, scans, Key Levels, alert history) and alert
    tools (create, list, update, delete, pause, resume; no orders or keys).
  * Saved alerts shared by the app, the MCP server and the new
    orbit-tape watch service (systemd user unit, off by default), with
    one program evaluating them at a time, catch-up of alerts missed while
    closed, and ntfy phone push as a second channel.
  * Daily routine: plan.toml with get_plan, market_snapshot, roman_setups
    (LIVE ranked, RAN for setups price already ran from, named levels,
    ready alert messages) and spot_status; the daily_report prompt and
    orbit-tape report with a daily timer (off by default), run with the
    plan's Claude model (sonnet by default) and a progress line.
  * Candle fetches retry HTTP 429; OKX perps and spot share one rate
    limiter; a series is fetched once per bar for all tools.
  * Indicators take an optional version. The app's Indicators panel and
    the MCP tools name installed copies older than the shipped ones, with
    the cp command that updates them. The .deb ships indicators/market.
  * Roman Setup 7.1: TradingView x_* setup values (checked against
    TradingView on OKX BTC and ETH); Roman ports are GPL-3.0-or-later.
  * Local-only defaults: Binance and OKX venues, a neutral scan list, the
    community indicator catalog, and data-server TLS verified unless
    turned off.

 -- atraxsrc <92285717+atraxsrc@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:10:00 +1100

